    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Coby Mayo** (66.72) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (66.01) headlining our offensive attack. Despite **Coby Mayo** facing a dangerous arm in McClanahan, the combination of a favorable hitter\u2019s park and the benefit of hitting in the #3 hole provides the highest efficiency ceiling on the board. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** remains an anchor in our 5x5 build, and while his matchup against Weathers carries a moderate SP_xERA, his projected volume and dynamic platoon advantage make him a lock. We are also monitoring **Gunnar Henderson** (64.35) closely; he benefits significantly from park factors today, though the 41% rain risk in his contest is a variable that could truncate his production should the game be delayed or shortened.\n\nMid-tier plays like **Liam Hicks** (59.93) and **Jackson Merrill** (58.98) represent our most significant \"Strong\" tier value drivers. **Liam Hicks** earns a notable boost from park factors and a dynamic platoon advantage against Young, despite the same rain concerns plaguing our middle infield. **Jackson Merrill** maintains a strong profile as a high-volume starter, and his utility is bolstered by his speed profile, which remains a priority for us in this league. **Wade Meckler** (52.78) and **Sam Antonacci** (51.59) are rostered primarily for their table-setting potential in the #1 spot, with **Sam Antonacci** receiving a marginal assist from wind conditions blowing out, helping him edge out competition for a starting spot.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision today involved **Nasim Nunez**, who finished just outside the active cut with a 47.64 score. While **Nasim Nunez** provides the elite sprint speed we covet, his projected efficiency simply could not overcome the higher scoring projections of our current starters, specifically in the context of the unfavorable #8 batting order position. We continue to hold **Andy Pages** on the IL, while players like **Heliot Ramos**, **Miguel Vargas**, **Jordan Westburg**, **Jacob Wilson**, **Josh Jung**, **Curtis Mead**, and **Dominic Smith** remain on the bench as we look to optimize our daily caps. Owners should be prepared for potential lineup shifts if the weather reports for the **Liam Hicks**, **Gunnar Henderson**, and **Coby Mayo** games worsen throughout the afternoon.",
